WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.292
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:09.153
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.453 --> 00:00:17.295
Unit thirty-six: Participle Adjectives (-ing / -ed). Today you will choose between boring and bored, interesting and interested.

4
00:00:17.595 --> 00:00:20.154
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.252
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:25.897
Boring.

7
00:00:26.883 --> 00:00:28.755
Boring means causing boredom.

8
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:30.699
The film was boring.

9
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:33.576
Your turn. Say: Boring.

10
00:00:36.433 --> 00:00:37.353
Boring.

11
00:00:38.117 --> 00:00:38.804
Bored.

12
00:00:39.817 --> 00:00:41.433
Bored means feeling boredom.

13
00:00:42.017 --> 00:00:43.215
I was bored.

14
00:00:43.817 --> 00:00:45.970
Your turn. Say: Bored.

15
00:00:48.833 --> 00:00:49.544
Bored.

16
00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.342
Interesting.

17
00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.593
Interesting means holding your attention.

18
00:00:55.183 --> 00:00:56.475
An interesting book.

19
00:00:57.083 --> 00:00:59.898
Your turn. Say: Interesting.

20
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:03.618
Interesting.

21
00:01:04.383 --> 00:01:05.384
Interested.

22
00:01:06.383 --> 00:01:08.429
Interested means wanting to know more.

23
00:01:09.017 --> 00:01:10.726
I am interested in art.

24
00:01:11.317 --> 00:01:13.737
Your turn. Say: Interested.

25
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:17.578
Interested.

26
00:01:18.317 --> 00:01:19.271
Exciting.

27
00:01:20.283 --> 00:01:22.411
Exciting means causing excitement.

28
00:01:23.017 --> 00:01:24.517
An exciting match.

29
00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.397
Your turn. Say: Exciting.

30
00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:31.258
Exciting.

31
00:01:32.017 --> 00:01:33.029
Excited.

32
00:01:34.017 --> 00:01:36.179
Excited means feeling excitement.

33
00:01:36.783 --> 00:01:38.017
We were excited.

34
00:01:38.617 --> 00:01:41.176
Your turn. Say: Excited.

35
00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:45.069
Excited.

36
00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:46.644
Tiring.

37
00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:49.696
Tiring means making you tired.

38
00:01:50.283 --> 00:01:51.610
A tiring journey.

39
00:01:52.217 --> 00:01:54.335
Your turn. Say: Tiring.

40
00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.097
Tiring.

41
00:01:58.850 --> 00:01:59.596
Tired.

42
00:02:00.583 --> 00:02:02.293
Tired means feeling tired.

43
00:02:02.883 --> 00:02:04.012
I am tired.

44
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:06.793
Your turn. Say: Tired.

45
00:02:09.633 --> 00:02:10.518
Tired.

46
00:02:11.333 --> 00:02:15.042
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:15.883 --> 00:02:19.497
Visal, describe a film with one -ing and one -ed adjective.

48
00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:31.272
The film was exciting, and I was excited. The -ing adjective describes the thing or person that causes the feeling. The -ed adjective describes the person who feels it.

49
00:02:32.383 --> 00:02:33.628
Give me another pair.

50
00:02:34.717 --> 00:02:44.802
The lesson was interesting, so the students were interested. The journey was tiring, so we were tired. A boring teacher makes bored students.

51
00:02:45.917 --> 00:02:47.545
What is a common mistake?

52
00:02:48.650 --> 00:03:00.241
Saying I am boring when I feel bored. I am boring means other people find me dull. Ask: Who feels it? Use -ed. What causes it? Use -ing.

53
00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.179
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:09.244
Grammar focus: Participle adjectives: -ing causes, -ed feels.

55
00:03:09.544 --> 00:03:10.754
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:12.950
The film was exciting.

57
00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.118
I was excited.

58
00:03:16.017 --> 00:03:17.424
The journey was tiring.

59
00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:23.794
-ing adjectives describe what causes the feeling. -ed adjectives describe the person who feels it.

60
00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:27.922
Be careful! Don't say: I am boring in this class.

61
00:03:29.867 --> 00:03:31.947
Say: I am bored in this class.

62
00:03:32.247 --> 00:03:33.794
Use -ed for a feeling.

63
00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.345
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:39.262
Cause or Feeling?.

65
00:03:39.562 --> 00:03:41.956
Last night I watched an exciting film.

66
00:03:42.967 --> 00:03:45.268
I was so excited that I could not sleep.

67
00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:49.358
The lesson was interesting, so the students were interested.

68
00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:52.900
The long journey was tiring, and we were tired.

69
00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.306
A boring speech made the audience bored.

70
00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:01.274
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:02.117 --> 00:04:03.489
The lesson was blank.

72
00:04:03.789 --> 00:04:07.454
A, interested. B, interesting. C, interest.

73
00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.232
The answer is B: interesting.

74
00:04:14.383 --> 00:04:15.826
I am blank in music.

75
00:04:16.126 --> 00:04:20.139
A, interested. B, interesting. C, interest.

76
00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.152
The answer is A: interested.

77
00:04:27.317 --> 00:04:29.618
The trip was blank, so I was exhausted.

78
00:04:29.918 --> 00:04:33.606
A, tired. B, tiring. C, tire.

79
00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:39.015
The answer is B: tiring.

80
00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:41.906
Which means 'I feel dull'?

81
00:04:42.206 --> 00:04:46.358
A, I am bored.. B, I am boring.. C, I am bore..

82
00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:52.143
The answer is A: I am bored..

83
00:04:53.283 --> 00:04:56.003
According to the reading, what could the writer not do?

84
00:04:56.303 --> 00:04:59.492
A, sleep. B, read. C, swim.

85
00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:04.963
The answer is A: sleep.

86
00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:09.423
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:10.283 --> 00:05:14.535
Describe a film using one -ing adjective and one -ed adjective.

88
00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:25.071
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:25.371 --> 00:05:36.640
The film was very exciting, and I was excited all the way through. The story was interesting, but my little brother was bored. I use -ing for the cause and -ed for the feeling.

90
00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.696
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:39.583 --> 00:05:45.800
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and participle adjectives: -ing causes, -ed feels.

92
00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:51.341
Today's value is appreciation of beauty. Learn to notice and value the beauty around you.

93
00:05:51.641 --> 00:05:55.385
See you in Unit thirty-seven. Goodbye!

94
00:05:55.685 --> 00:05:58.372
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

